{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/pulls/318","id":5069442747,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVWRcjM8AAAABLimOuw","html_url":"https://github.com/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/pull/318","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/pull/318.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/pull/318.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/issues/318","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/pulls/318/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/pulls/318/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/issues/318/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmegaSoftDLL/lume/statuses/28029b411038e38a52cdafe555c7a15b9214a366","number":318,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(stdlib): implement Track L standard library & domains (#257)","user":{"login":"OmegaSoftDLL","id":215607367,"node_id":"U_kgDODNnoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/215607367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL","html_url":"https://github.com/OmegaSoftDLL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmegaSoftDLL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nImplements and run-verifies all 6 **Track L — Standard library & domains (#257)** frontiers from docs/33-build-anything-plan.md, held to docs/28-delivery-rules.md §7 (AGENTS.md #7):\n\n1. **Networking (compiler/stage1/net.src + compiler/stage1/lume/05_codegen.src)**:\n   - Native Linux x86-64 socket syscalls (\net_tcp_listen, \net_tcp_connect, \net_tcp_accept, \net_udp_bind, \net_udp_sendto, \net_send_str, \net_recv_str, \net_close).\n   - IPv4 address/CIDR subnet routing, RFC 1071 16-bit one's-complement checksum, UDP/TCP packet builder & tamper detection, TCP 3-way handshake & teardown FSM, TLS 1.3 HKDF-Expand-Label key schedule & AEAD record layer with authentication tag tamper rejection, HTTP/1.1 parser & serializer, and real Linux kernel loopback TCP HTTP/1.1 & UDP socket exchanges (\net_http_loopback_exchange, \net_udp_loopback_exchange).\n\n2. **Async I/O Runtime (compiler/stage1/async_rt.src + compiler/stage1/lume/05_codegen.src)**:\n   - Native Linux epoll syscalls (epoll_create_fd, epoll_add_in, epoll_wait_one) and real OS pipe readiness wakeup (\reactor_epoll_pipe_exchange).\n   - Readiness I/O reactor, deadline-ordered timer wheel, bounded max_inflight backpressure admission control, and multi-worker work-stealing scheduler (ws_pool_new, ws_step, ws_run_all).\n   - Removes redundant record-mock promise_*/signal_* helpers from compiler/stage1/concurrency.src in favor of compiler-native promise[T] and signal[T].\n\n3. **GUI & 2D Graphics (compiler/stage1/gui.src)**:\n   - 2D RGBA software framebuffer rasterizer (canvas_new, canvas_set_px, canvas_get_px, canvas_fill_rect), Porter-Duff source-over RGB alpha blending (canvas_blend_rgb), declarative \u000bbox/hbox layout solver, spatial hit-testing & click dispatch, and Netpbm P3 .ppm & .svg vector frame encoders.\n\n4. **Database (compiler/stage1/db.src)**:\n   - Multi-level B+Tree storage index with page splitting (\btree_insert_node, \btree_delete_node, \btree_get, \btree_height, \btree_range_scan, \btree_verify_invariant), ACID transactions with MVCC snapshot isolation (db_begin_tx, db_put, db_delete, db_commit_tx, db_rollback_tx, db_snapshot_read), cost-based query planner (IndexPointSeek, IndexRangeScan, SequentialScan), and WAL encoder.\n\n5. **Media (compiler/stage1/media.src)**:\n   - RIFF/WAV 16-bit PCM audio container encoder & decoder (wav_encode_pcm16, wav_decode_pcm16), 3-tap FIR low-pass DSP filter (^Gudio_fir3_lowpass), lossless RLE (media_rle_encode, media_rle_decode), and inter-frame video GOP (I-frame + P-frame temporal residual delta) codec (\u000bideo_encode_gop, \u000bideo_decode_gop).\n\n6. **Real ML (compiler/stage1/nn.src, compiler/stage1/ai_runtime.src, compiler/stage1/lume/06b_phase3.src, compiler/stage1/lcaas.src)**:\n   - Extends compiler symbolic autodiff (grad, \u000balue_and_grad, jvp, \u000bjp) beyond polynomials to differentiate \relu(u), sq(u), cube(u), ^Gbs(u), clamp(u, lo, hi), leaky_relu(u, k), and quot(a, b) via chain/quotient rules while diagnosing unknown calls with [N0400].\n   - Adds reverse-mode Wengert tape autodiff (^Gd_tape_new, ^Gd_var, ^Gd_add, ^Gd_sub, ^Gd_mul_milli, ^Gd_div_milli, ^Gd_relu, ^Gd_tanh_milli, ^Gd_sigmoid_milli, ^Gd_exp_milli, ^Gd_backward, ^Gd_grad_of) and safetensors binary frame + onnx verifiers in \nn.src.\n   - Adds Hamiltonian Monte Carlo (infer_hmc, hmc_leapfrog, prob_grad_log_lik) with symplectic leapfrog integration and Metropolis energy acceptance in ^Gi_runtime.src.\n\nCloses #257\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-29T14:03:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T17:09:08Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T17:09:05Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T17:09:05Z","merge_commit_sha":"ce7842679f9bfc8b67acaf604fd254e005646210","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"OmegaSoftDLL:feat/l-stdlib-domains-257","ref":"feat/l-stdlib-domains-257","repo":{"id":1432640652,"node_id":"R_kgDOVWRcjA","name":"lume"